QuizAI – Smart Quiz Generator Android App

QuizAI is an Android app built with Kotlin and Jetpack Compose. It allows users to generate topic-based quizzes, attempt them in a beautiful modern UI, and view detailed results with full history tracking.

Note: This project is still under active development, and some planned features are not fully completed yet.

Features

• Dynamic quiz generation based on user-selected topic, difficulty, question count, subtopics, and optional custom instructions.
• Clean Jetpack Compose quiz interface with question progress, next/previous navigation, and submit confirmation.
• Detailed result screen showing animated score circle, performance message, summary breakdown, and full answer review.
• Local history saving using Room Database, including topic, difficulty, date, score, and wrong answers.
• History screen with list of past attempts, delete option, and detailed view for each attempt.
• Home screen with recent results section and navigation drawer.
• Dark theme toggle, clear history option, about dialog, and app info footer.

Tech Stack

• Kotlin
• Jetpack Compose
• ViewModel + StateFlow architecture
• Room Database (Quiz attempts + wrong answers)
• Retrofit network layer
• Material 3 components
• Navigation Compose
• Light / Dark theming with smooth UI

Project Structure (High-Level)

• Screens: Home, Generate Quiz, Quiz Questions, Results, History, Attempt Details
• Data Layer: Entities, DAOs, Database, Repository
• ViewModels: GenerateQuiz, QuizQuestion, QuizResult, QuizHistory
• Navigation: NavHost + Screen routes

Getting Started

Clone the repository.

Open it in Android Studio.

Let Gradle sync automatically.

Connect a device/emulator.

Press Run to launch the app.

Current Status

The app is fully functional but still being refined.
Upcoming improvements include better UI polish, extra analytics, more customization options, and enhanced user experience handling.

